.TH ACCT 2 "2026-02-28" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
acct \- switch process accounting on or off
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, -lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int acct(const char *" filename ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B acct()
system call enables or disables process accounting. If called with the name of an existing file as its argument, accounting is turned on, and records for each terminating process are appended to
.IR filename .
If
.I filename
is NULL, accounting is turned off.
A relative
.I filename
is resolved from the caller's working directory.
Turning accounting on with a new file stops writing to the old one.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned. On error, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EACCES
.I filename
is not a regular file.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I filename
points outside the accessible address space.
.TP
.B ENOENT
.I filename
does not exist.
.TP
.B EPERM
The caller is not the superuser.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intro(2)
